🪄
"MagicWords"/en
=== start
¶Say a color or a feeling out loud and the stage obeys your words.¶

¶Only the last three words count, so each new spell replaces the last, and
lowercasing means Red and red are the same spell. This listens in English
because the magic words are English.¶
spell: Speech(language: 'en-US' limit: 3).🔡()

¶Whether a word was one of the last three said. Splitting on spaces first means
saying spread doesn't count as saying red.¶
ƒ said(word•'')•? spell.segment(' ').has(word)

sky: said('red') ? Color.red
	said('blue') ? Color.blue
		said('green') ? Color.green
			Color.white

mood: said('happy') ? "😄"
	said('sad') ? "😢"
		said('sleepy') ? "😴"
			"😐"

Stage(
	[
		Group(
			Stack('|' 1m)
			[
				Phrase(mood 8m resting: said('spin') ? Sequence.spin() ø)
				Phrase(spell = '' ? "say red, blue, green, happy, sad, sleepy, or spin" spell 0.75m)
			]
		)
	]
	background: sky
)
